{
  "id": "remint-word-status",
  "title": "Re-mint: the status of a word created in the window is re-minted at its estimated time",
  "covers": [
    "re-mint step 1c (SYNC.md 10.4): word.status_set / word.status_cleared whose entry_seq is the entry of a note created in the window is window-derived: re-minted with mint_at, same payload",
    "a word status of an entry with no window note stays an edit of a shared register: discarded"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Before A goes offline, B marks entries 3000001 and 3000002 ignored (seq 1-2).",
    "A's clock jumps 10 days ahead; offline, A adds word 3000001 (note + card) and a minute later marks it known; A also marks 3000002 known (no note on A).",
    "A pushes with the clock still wrong: note.created and both word.status_set are clock_ahead; card.created is unknown_reference.",
    "Re-mint: the status of 3000001 is window-derived (its seq is the entry of a note in W): re-minted with mint_at(t'), so it carries the real time and beats B's earlier choice, as if A's clock had been right. The status of 3000002 names no window note: discarded (in the discard list); B's ignored stands.",
    "A also reviewed the new card an hour after creating it (unknown_reference). It is re-minted in step 6b with a new id and reviewed_at shifted by the same delta as the creations, so it stays an hour after its card. `remint` lists the inputs; tools/validate.py recomputes the selection and the shift."
  ],
